# RETIRED as of STEP B (#177) -- kept for history, not applied.
#
# The `.retired` extension is deliberate: `kubectl apply -f pantry-bot/` (or
# any *.yaml glob) silently skips this file now, so there's no risk of
# accidentally re-creating a claim the Deployment no longer references.
#
# The bot's Deployment (40-deployment.yaml) now uses an emptyDir restored
# from the R2/Litestream replica on every start, not this PVC -- that's what
# lets the pod actually reschedule onto a different node. See that file's
# STEP B comments and #177 for the full migration record.
#
# IMPORTANT: the PVC this file used to create (`pantry-bot-data`) may still
# exist in the cluster with real historical data on it, orphaned now that
# nothing references it. Do NOT `kubectl delete pvc pantry-bot-data` casually
# -- leave it as an extra safety net until the emptyDir+restore path has been
# running in production long enough to fully trust (a real failover test,
# not just a manual restore check). Deleting it destroys that fallback
# permanently and it cannot be recreated from anywhere else.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Original file content and rationale below, preserved as-is.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Persistent storage for pantry-bot's SQLite database.
#
# Replaces the named Docker volume `pantry-bot_pantry-data` mounted at /data.
#
# This is the one PVC in the whole migration where corruption is unrecoverable
# — it holds live user data with no upstream source to re-derive it from.
# Two properties protect it:
#
#   1. `strategy: Recreate` on the Deployment. SQLite in WAL mode tolerates
#      multiple readers/writers only through a shared filesystem lock; two pods
#      on the same volume across a rolling update is exactly the scenario that
#      produces a corrupt WAL. Recreate guarantees the old pod is fully gone.
#   2. ReadWriteOnce + single node. The second pod could not mount it anyway.
#
# The directory contains pantry.db plus pantry.db-wal and pantry.db-shm while
# the DB is open. All three must be copied together, from a STOPPED database —
# copying pantry.db alone from a running bot yields a DB missing every committed
# transaction still in the WAL.
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: pantry-bot-data
  namespace: pantry-bot
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: pantry-bot
    app.kubernetes.io/part-of: homelab
spec:
  accessModes: ["ReadWriteOnce"]
  storageClassName: local-path
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 1Gi
